From: Onigiri
Subject: [PATCH] Save cover selfies as previewed

"Save selfies as previewed" did nothing on the cover: Camera shoots with the
rear lenses there (0006), and only the preview mirrors (0007), so pictures
and videos still saved unflipped. With the setting on, flip them on the
preview's axis the way stock QuickShot does: a sensor flip, which the HAL
keeps off the preview and needs before it honors the pictures' scaler flip,
and a MediaRecorder flip for videos. Where the flip lands sideways to the
saved orientation it would read upside down, so turn the picture or video
half a turn more, as stock does. Motion photo clips take the motion photo
maker's flip, as QuickShot's do. That flip is horizontal, so under a
vertical one the clip turns half a turn more than the picture, as stock's
processing path already does for a vertical scaler flip. The sensor flip
is a session key; Camera opens a new session when it comes back from its
settings, so the switch applies there.

